From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Start the stream helper as a child process inside a Flatpak sandbox

The daemon starts every stream as a transient systemd user unit. From inside
a Flatpak sandbox that asks the host's systemd to run a path that exists only
in the sandbox, so no stream can ever start.

When /.flatpak-info exists, the daemon now runs the helper itself with
GSubprocess. It keeps a table from unit name to process, and StopStream sends
that process SIGTERM, the signal systemd would have sent. StartStream still
returns a unit name in the same format, so the D-Bus interface is unchanged.
The child receives that name as ND_STREAM_UNIT, which lets a client check
whether its stream is still running without systemd.

The helper path is now taken from the build prefix rather than fixed at
/usr/libexec, since a Flatpak installs it under /app. Outside a sandbox
nothing changes.

diff -ruN a/src/meson.build b/src/meson.build
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -141,7 +141,9 @@
 if build_daemon
   executable('gnome-network-displays-daemon',
     gnome_nd_daemon_sources,
-    c_args: ['-DND_NO_GTK'],
+    c_args: ['-DND_NO_GTK',
+             '-DND_STREAM_HELPER="@0@"'.format(join_paths(get_option('prefix'), 'libexec',
+                                                          'gnome-network-displays-stream'))],
     dependencies: gnome_nd_daemon_deps,
     install: true,
     link_with: [wfd_server, cc_cast_channel],
diff -ruN a/src/nd-manager.c b/src/nd-manager.c
--- a/src/nd-manager.c
+++ b/src/nd-manager.c
@@ -36,6 +36,11 @@
 
